            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    .container-border1 {\r\n        border: 2px solid #ccc;\r\n        border-radius: 15px;\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n\r\n        background-color: white;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .flex-container {\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        justify-content: center;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .flex-child:first-child {\r\n        margin-right: 20px;\r\n\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    .flex-child2 {\r\n        margin-right: 20px;\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    @media (max-width: 800px) {\r\n        .flex-container {\r\n            flex-direction: column;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .circle {\r\n            width: 25px;\r\n            height: 25px;\r\n            border-radius: 50%;\r\n            box-sizing: border-box;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            display: inline-block;\r\n            line-height: 25px;\r\n            background-color: #9e2065;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .circle a {\r\n            text-decoration: none;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/course_1.png\">\r\n     <span style=\"font-size:2em\"> Add Seaming Stitches <a data-GlossaryId='605' class='glossaryhelp'><i class='fa fa-question-circle-o' aria-hidden='true'></i></a></span><br>Because the hand knit pattern is written to be knit in the round, when we knit the body and sleeves we need to add a seaming stitch.<br><em> At a gauge of 4 stitches to the inch, if you don't add a stitch on each side of the front and back, your sweater can be a full 1\" smaller than you planned.</em>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n    <span style=\"font-size:2em\">\r\n        <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/course_2.png\"> Upside Down Ribbing\r\n    </span><br>Knitting top down and finishing the hems with ribbing means we need to bind off in ribbing. Many knitters avoid doing this.<br>\r\n    <div class=\"flex-container\">\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"flex-child\">\r\n            <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Easy Ribber Bind Off\" data-vimeoid=\"151857401\">\r\n                <figure><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/680394459-c2254b7c45521ee31952031c97c8cfd372fd6c1625dbaf623a2bf58e79939a8f-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n                    <figcaption align=\"center\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Easy Ribber Bind Off</figcaption>\r\n                </figure>\r\n\r\n            </div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"flex-child2\">\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"videopopup\" data-videotitle=\"Stretchiest Bind Off Ever!\" data-vimeoid=\"151858299\">\r\n                <figure> <img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/564146402-c0bd06d49fdf54aed630d489f4cb46357345cf52f5c49e24c51d36c314a92a40-d_1280x720?r=pad\">\r\n                    <figcaption align=\"center\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Stretchy Sewn Bind Off (Backstitch Bind off)</figcaption>\r\n                </figure>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div><br>\r\n<div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n\r\n\r\n    <b><span style=\"font-size:2em\">\r\n            <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/course_3.png\"> For the Perfectionist: Graft the ribbing to the sleeve\r\n        </span></b><br>\r\n    <ul>\r\n        <li>Cast on for your ribbing with a tubular cast on.</li>\r\n\r\n        <li>Knit your ribbing</li>\r\n        <li>Transfer the stitches to the main bed</li>\r\n        <li>Knit a few rows in stockinette</li>\r\n        <li>Scrap off</li><br>\r\n\r\n        <li>Scrap off the sleeve and neatly <a data-GlossaryId='521' class='glossaryhelp'>Kitchener Join<i class='fa fa-question-circle' aria-hidden='true'></i></a> the sleeve and the ribbing</li>\r\n        <br></ul>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div class=\"container-border1\">\r\n    <span style=\"font-size:2em\">\r\n       <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/course_4.png\"> Twisted Stitches\r\n    </span><br>\r\n\r\n    \r\n         In knitting our sample, Instead of scrapping off the yoke stitches, I removed them on a strand of yarn.\r\n            This was a mistake. it made it difficult to rehang the stitches without twisting them.<br><em> Lesson Learned: Even when hand knitting, take time to scrap off. This will ensure the stitches are easier to hang and will not be twisted.</em>\r\n            <figure><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/101/twisted1.jpg\">\r\n                <figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Stitches twisted when re-hanging them.</figcaption>\r\n            </figure>\r\n        \r\n        \r\n            <figure><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/101/twisted.jpg\">\r\n                <figcaption align=\"center\"><br>Stitches held on a yarn strand made it difficult to rehang them without twisting.</figcaption>\r\n            </figure>\r\n        \r\n    \r\n</div>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 8491,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Lessons Learned",
          "slug": "lessons-learned",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
